HB0189HS001/ADOPTED
Page 2-line 3 After "minor" insert "or purported minor".
Page 4-line 13 After "minor" insert "or purported minor".
Page 4-line 21 After "(ii)" insert "Except as provided by subsection
(h) of this section,".
Page 5-line 14 After "($5,000.00)" insert ", or both".
Page 5-line 18 After "($10,000.00)" insert ", or both".
Page 5-line 23 After "($20,000.00)" insert ", or both".
Page 6-line 8 After "minors" insert "or purported minors".
Page 6-lines 10 through 12 Delete entirely and insert:
"(f) A minor victim, or the minor's parent or legal guardian acting on
behalf of the minor, may bring a civil cause of action under this section for
damages and any other relief the court deems reasonable. The ability of a parent
or legal guardian to bring a civil action on behalf of the minor shall not
preclude the minor from bringing an action independently upon reaching the age
of majority. This civil cause of action is independent of criminal proceedings
and may be brought by the minor or the minor's parent or legal guardian
regardless of whether criminal charges have been filed. A civil cause of action
under this section shall not be contingent upon a conviction in a criminal
case.".
Page 6-after line 18 Insert:
"(h) The provisions of this section shall not apply to consensual
communication between a person who is not less than eighteen (18) years of age
and a minor who is not more than four (4) years younger than the person if:

(i) The communication does not involve coercion, exploitation or
manipulation of the minor; and
(ii) The communication occurs within the context of a consensual
dating or romantic relationship.". WASHUT, CHAIRMAN
HB0189HW001/ADOPTED
Page 6-line 16 Delete "a bona fide" and insert "any age-appropriate
sex education curriculum or program at any church,";
after "university" insert ".".
Page 6-lines 17 and 18 Delete entirely. CHESTEK
HB0189HW002/ADOPTED
Page 6-after line 18 Delete the standing committee amendment (HB0189HS001/A)
to this line and insert:
"(h) Nothing in this section shall require law enforcement to notify the
parent or legal guardian of a minor who reports a violation or is the victim of
a violation of this section, or any other connected violation of Wyoming law,
if the parent or guardian is alleged to have been a party to the violation or
law enforcement believes the parent or guardian will interfere with the
investigation.
(j) This section shall not apply to a minor's spouse if a judge of a court
of record in Wyoming has approved the marriage, the minor's parent or legal
guardian has provided consent for the marriage, or the minor is emancipated, as
specified in W.S. 20-1-102(b) through (d).".
To the extent required by this amendment: renumber as necessary. LIEN
